      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(mcp): open App views from channel replies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMCP App tool results already render inline in Control UI, but channel turns lose that interactive view. Telegram, Slack, Discord, and text-only transports preserve the assistant text yet provide no way to open the latest successful App view.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis carries only the latest successful view identity through the agent result, then materializes one portable `web-app` presentation action after the final visible reply has been normalized. The Gateway mints the existing standalone-view ticket at that last moment, bounds it to the live view lease, and uses one lifecycle-owned HTTPS origin prepared by Tailscale Serve or Funnel. Channel adapters retain transport ownership; prerequisite #111116 keeps Telegram's native `web_app` button DM-only and falls back to the portable HTTPS action elsewhere.\n\nControl UI remains unchanged and receives no duplicate action. Missing origin, capacity, lease, transport support, or an expired view leaves the original reply text intact. The action contains only a fixed label and opaque URL; App HTML, input/result data, session identity, view metadata, and bearer credentials are not serialized into channel payloads.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can open the latest MCP App from the final assistant reply in Telegram DMs, Slack, and Discord. Other transports keep an understandable text-and-link fallback. Tailscale Serve links remain tailnet-only; Funnel links are internet-reachable. Existing reply text and Control UI behavior are preserved.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 554 focused agent/runtime, MCP host, Telegram, Slack, and Discord tests passed after the agent registry rebase.\n- Browser conformance passed twice consecutively after a reproducible cold-start Chromium navigation retry.\n- Full changed gate, private-QA build, and canonical package tarball integrity passed on Blacksmith Testbox: [run 29672729609](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29672729609).\n- Latest-base adapter/materialization proof passed: [run 29673533108](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29673533108).\n- Exact pushed-head agent-runner/materialization proof passed: [run 29673634946](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29673634946).\n- Fresh autoreview after the final rebase reported no actionable findings (0.93 confidence).\n- The credentialed exact-head Telegram Desktop/Mini App Crabbox workflow will be attached before merge and must prove button receipt/open, official-SDK fixture rendering, app-only tool invocation, resource read, and expired state.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I understand and reviewed the full owner/caller/callee/channel surface and addressed the accepted autoreview finding before opening this PR.\n",
